   {
    "id": "p_00052",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The following example shows how to create a directory named [B46]/home/cnd/mod1[/B46], with read/write/search permissions for owner\nand group, and with read/search permissions for others.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B46": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00053",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A47][/A47]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A47": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_338_07\" id=\"tag_17_338_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00054",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00055",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A48][/A48]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A48": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_338_08\" id=\"tag_17_338_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00056",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I49]mkdir[/I49]() function originated in 4.2 BSD and was added to System V in Release 3.0.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I49": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00057",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "4.3 BSD detects [ENAMETOOLONG].",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00058",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The POSIX.1-1990 standard required that the group ID of a newly created directory be set to the group ID of its parent directory\nor to the effective group ID of the creating process. FIPS 151-2 required that implementations provide a way to have the group ID\nbe set to the group ID of the containing directory, but did not prohibit implementations also supporting a way to set the group ID\nto the effective group ID of the creating process. Conforming applications should not assume which group ID will be used. If it\nmatters, an application can use [A50][I51]chown[/I51]()[/A50] to set the group ID after the directory is\ncreated, or determine under what conditions the implementation will set the desired group ID.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A50": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/chown.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I51": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00059",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The purpose of the [I52]mkdirat[/I52]() function is to create a directory in directories other than the current working directory\nwithout exposure to race conditions. Any part of the path of a file could be changed in parallel to the call to [I53]mkdir[/I53](),\nresulting in unspecified behavior. By opening a file descriptor for the target directory and using the [I54]mkdirat[/I54]() function it\ncan be guaranteed that the newly created directory is located relative to the desired directory.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I52": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I53": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00060",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Implementations are encouraged to have [I55]mkdir[/I55]() and [I56]mkdirat[/I56]() report an [EILSEQ] error if the last component of\n[I57]path[/I57] contains any bytes that have the encoded value of a &lt;newline&gt; character.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I55": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I56": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I57": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00061",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     47
    ],
    "text": "[A58][/A58]FUTURE DIRECTIONS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A58": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_338_09\" id=\"tag_17_338_09\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00062",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     49,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00063",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     51
    ],
